s. Production-interface host regressions must exercise reload before reveal, during confirmation and during delayed issuance; the replacement page must receive no surviving disclosure authority, stale confirmation must apply nothing, and no mutation may be replayed.\",\n    \"R2 — tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py:333 and :336; tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c39.py:602: the C31 replacement mapping overstates assertion coverage. C31-N01 maps solely to C39-N01, which checks Runtime topics and board presentation but does not enforce the required Gateway key restrictions or several other inventory assertions. C31-N04 maps solely to C39-N02's review geometry/apply checks, omitting its accessibility obligations; useful existing C31 observations and C39-N04 results are not required by that mapping. Acceptance: preserve each unretired C31 obligation in an enforced assertion-level mapping. Correctly scope the Gateway Keys/detail negative assertions, require the existing same-bundle checks that establish the accessibility facts, and retain source-bound evidence for missing assertions. Qualification must reject removal or failure of those assertions; preserve historical failed records.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [\n    \"E1 — docs/planning/evidence/P09/native/cumulative/C31/native-acceptance.json retains C31-N01 as failed with gateway_no_version=false. The replacement C39-N01 does not test Gateway key actions; C39-N03 checks the Keys table and key-kind controls without asserting that Gateway row details exclude Issue additional key and Finish rotation. The retained evidence therefore does not establish this mandatory C31 native restriction. This is an evidence gap, not proof that the product offers forbidden actions. Passing component tests do not replace the missing native assertion.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/admin/review-sheet.tsx:265: derive the header state pill from the rotation stage when showing a rotation. The retained issued and completed rotation captures both show Draft beside the title despite the panel reporting the actual completed operation.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Recomputed all four supplied fingerprints. All 5,031 scoped file hashes matched initially and at final recheck. Independently verified current membership and content of all 18,338 compiled-input entries, identical check inventories, build flags and all 18 recorded check-log hashes. Hash consistency does not independently authenticate compiler execution or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Recomputed the complete 1,621-entry fixture-bundle hash, including executable modes and symlink targets, and verified its executable and bundle identifier against preparation. The six frozen prototype files also match their manifest. No fresh build, test suite, native interaction, endpoint call, credential access or OS permission grant was performed.\",\n    \"The reload finding follows the inspected production lifecycle and authority paths; it was not independently reproduced by driving or reloading the application during this read-only review.\",\n    \"Retained logs report 550 renderer tests and all 15 ui_v2_reviews production-interface tests passing. Inspected tests cover typed confirmation, tenant retirement, delayed settlement, unknown outcomes, reconciliation, storage recovery, stable timestamps and operation-ID reuse after relaunch. These results do not exercise the renderer-teardown defect.\",\n    \"Inspected current C31/C39 native records, observations, retained AX trees and representative rotation/parity captures. C31-N02/N03 support typed review and staged rotation behavior. Raw C31-N01/N04 failures remain preserved; their supersession does not itself prove equivalent assertion coverage. Spoken VoiceOver output and signed installed-release behavior were not established.\",\n    \"Verified C30 predecessor record, request, receipt, audit and owner-decision hashes. C30 is accepted