{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/native-lifecycle-review-boundary.md docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/qualification-rationale.md docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/driver-amendment-01/failed-native-attempt/failure.json docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/driver-amendment-01/old-red.json docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/driver-amendment-01/new-green.json docs/planning/evidence/C31/remediation-attempt-05/reload-lifecycle/notes.md docs/planning/evidence/C31/remediation-attempt-05/reload-lifecycle/source-bindings.json'","aggregated_output":"# Native lifecycle inspection boundary for the independent C31 review\n\nThe four focused regressions exercise actual Host/Tauri IPC and the production\ncore with scripted native adapters. They establish reload before reveal, after\na native confirmation is held, during delayed issuance, and the delivery/other\nwindow control. They do not exercise AppKit event-task scheduling or a\nRevealSecret effect concurrent with native page teardown.\n\nThe independent reviewer should inspect that remaining production boundary:\n`authority.rs` dispatch releases the state lock before running effects, including\n`Effect::RevealSecret`. `NativeSecrets::reveal` queues an AppKit task; its reveal\nownership generation is allocated inside that task. `NativeSecrets::dismiss`\nends the current sheet. `NativeConfirmation::confirm` also queues presentation;\n`present` constructs a sheet after obtaining its main window. The pinned local\nTauri runtime-wry 2.12.2 implementation of `Context::send_user_message` executes\na task inline on its main thread and enqueues it from other threads.\n\nThese are static observations, not an executed race reproduction or an\nindependent verdict. No additional native UI action was performed during the\nsealed fixture queue. Determine whether the production ordering preserves the\nrequired page-exit ownership under queued/admitted callbacks, and report any\nactual remaining fix honestly. Neither a favorable score nor the current four\nfocused results should be represented as coverage of an unexecuted AppKit race.\nThis concerns C31 only; it does not reopen C30.\n# C31 remediation qualification\n\nThe owner closed C30 at all nine on 2026-11-02. Its raw attempt12 remains fail at 9/9/9/8/8 and its audit remains false. No C30 code, coverage, timing, captures, mapping or re-review is performed. Historical G7 performance remains historical; it does not describe the new executable. C41 retains its existing explicit override.\n\nC31 attempt05 was actually accepted at 9/8/8/8/8 with R1/R2/E1 retained. The two explicit collaborator commits are integrated as eac6d07f (native page-lifetime retirement) and 1dda32c7 (enforced native inventory/accessibility coverage). Original old-red/new-green records remain unchanged. The first integrated preflight was denied local fixture bind by the sandbox; fresh preflight02 passed with normal local networking. No behavioral failure is hidden by that retry.\n\nThe production Host lifecycle and native acceptance helpers changed. The current P09 contract requires all19 mapped native drivers and all18 current repository checks on the new application and compiled inputs. Those execute once after all focused preflight and source sealing, with C36/C43 first and C44 last. C31-N01/N04 now must pass their own assertions plus current C39 targets; historical failed raw records remain unchanged. No new C30 timing hook runs. All non-C31 source is unchanged except the explicitly listed additive administrative provenance tools.\n\nC29 attempt10 stays historical actual full9 on G7; broad shared-file scope does not imply a new current C29 verdict. New C31 and cumulative P09 reviews inspect every declared source/provenance change. Current independent C31/C32/P09 gates remain full9. No phase score, unrun check, controller completion, live call, release or publication is inferred.\n\nThe guest Terminal-owned qualification supervisor holds an exclusive OS lock, records source and Terminal ancestry, checks exact source/HEAD and full bundle at driver boundaries, checks foreground ownership, writes fresh raw logs and per-driver results, and stops on a real failure. A model exit does not own its process. Valid completed stages are retained; incomplete evidence never silently passes or starts a duplicate writer.\n{\n  \"time\": \"2026-11-02T13:06:33.321694+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"failed driver before acceptance\",\n  \"error\": \"scoped Gateway key-kind node missing; workspace must be explicitly chosen before Keys controls appear\",\n  \"driver_log_sha256\": \"2dfb6218d2b4a3134eeada22cb1196d9ac054671e26d011111305887728933d4\",\n  \"no_native_verdict\": true,\n  \"completed_valid_drivers\": 10,\n  \"application_unchanged\": true\n}\n{\n  \"command\": [\n    \"python3\",\n    \"-B\",\n    \"tools/native-acceptance/test_administration_coverage.py\",\n    \"GatewayWorkspacePrerequisite\",\n    \"-v\"\n  ],\n  \"exit\": 1,\n  \"log\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/driver-amendment-01/old-red-recorded.log\",\n  \"log_sha256\": \"c5b9e0b8b1865d6cbcb0470bbb7bbf6f8a0a3fe6fbf20c4049579fcda8c84eea\",\n  \"meaning\": \"Original integrated driver fails at exact missing scoped key control before workspace selection; no UI or app operation\"\n}\n{\n  \"command\": [\n    \"python3\",\n    \"-B\",\n    \"tools/native-acceptance/test_administration_coverage.py\",\n    \"-v\"\n  ],\n  \"exit\": 0,\n  \"log\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/driver-amendment-01/new-green.log\",\n  \"log_sha256\": \"82733dd2f7ed62b3473dad6f2f00591c9b788b8ea0c0d25c379fdc4f92cd5d1d\"\n}\n# C31 attempt-05 R1 — native renderer lifecycle\n\nThe native main-page lifecycle now retires its delivery nonce and configuration review/confirmation, forgets held keys, marks unsettled issuances forgotten-on-settle, dismisses disclosure, and publishes current state. It preserves the active business context, admitted work and remote outcomes. Ordinary delivery-session recovery and secondary-webview retirement preserve the live main-page review/disclosure.\n\nFour focused host production-interface tests exercise the existing `Host::retire_webview` callback and real Tauri IPC against a synthetic localhost TLS management service. Unmodified application sources failed all three reload assertions: held secret survived, pending review survived, and delayed-issued key became Held. The delivery/secondary-window control passed. Original source copies and `old-red-build-01` preserve this actual result.\n\nAfter the native fix, `new-green-01` reached the correct lifecycle states but its later refusal assertions exposed a test helper error: Tauri returns domain refusal in an `outcome: refusal` JSON envelope, not an IPC command error. The helper was corrected to parse the production envelope; no application change was made between green01 and green02. The original red assertions precede those later helper checks and remain unchanged.\n\n`new-green-02`: all four tests passed (1.82s execution). They prove reload before Reveal, reload during native confirmation, reload while the original issuance is dispatched but its response pending, refusal of old/new-page disclosure, no stale confirmation write, preserved completed outcome and rotation facts, exactly one issuance, and an explicit fresh review that still applies. The fourth control proves delivery recovery alone and another webview do not revoke the main page's still-live disclosure. Focused formatting and whitespace checks passed; the test target compiled without warnings.\n\nNo full Rust check suite, repository suite, app bundle build, native gate, product endpoint, actual AppKit interaction or live credential was used. All raw failed attempts are retained. Existing performance/native evidence remains historical on its original bytes; this focused remediation makes no claim that it qualified a rebuilt bundle. C30 is outside this change and remains owner-closed.\n{\n  \"baseline\": \"fd649dd8606380ebbd5d4d7646395492c676fa52\",\n  \"original_source_hashes\": {\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs\": \"d5e9afbfe7ce3f8eb0ff833b8a9267c4576db7bb854e6c799bea9a220ddfac53\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs\": \"629dec32b59a6b674aa1442ece0e3f44d9b8ab7ba1efd2b5ae1671d9b35899ab\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/change_domain.rs\": \"ced8bcfa43b04c94828dfefe62d06e00eff473e63a7c1cce564eceffd55d9869\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/delivery.rs\": \"f9dfcb7a50d08c1b03f55c0a7e907c048f5aece62e783882fa6fcd0ded8ed8bb\"\n  },\n  \"current_source_hashes\": {\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml\": \"e051d6781c547d0b1e9af95543926d03db46bfa373e5c53d915351b11435cc2a\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs\": \"38f53eff45ffab6ae9d90f1ce24b1d9658ea3359d8f9443e6f1ff13cd4cb044c\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/tests/renderer_review_lifecycle.rs\": \"b32142833ab86a0c68f438dcd2874cedcd69322e98a475f5e7b8d47354e3007a\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs\": \"9b0be4597094d9f0a747283a833619f163b81dcbacf283ce8949955a38f2ebcb\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/change_domain.rs\": \"dc7ecc9b53265f66a34f5bf6fddd5fe90a7136b6e36fbbbd4d0e85ceeb89c726\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/delivery.rs\": \"456da052f69296ddd4bb682739a4b10ef42f8441347910f37f6de7bb62dd9ba8\"\n  },\n  \"recorded_utc\": \"2026-11-02T12:01:51.614886+00:00\",\n  \"actual_tests\": \"3 bug cases fail original source, all4 focused tests pass corrected source; exact rawlogs preserved\",\n  \"scope\": \"C31 attempt05 R1 only; no C30 work/full suites/native gates/bundle\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
