{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' apps/desktop/src/v2/modal.tsx; sed -n '1,210p' apps/desktop/src/features/administration/runtime-changes.tsx; sed -n '250,370p' apps/desktop/src/features/administration/runtime-changes.tsx\"","aggregated_output":"import { useEffect, useId, useRef, type KeyboardEvent, type ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport { useShellStore } from './store'\n\ninterface ModalProps {\n    label: string\n    onClose: () => void\n    children: ReactNode\n    /** Width in CSS px (default 560). */\n    width?: number\n    /** Inner padding in CSS px (default 20); 0 for a dialog that lays itself out edge to edge. */\n    padding?: number\n    /** Distance from the top of the window in CSS px (default 4vh); the prototype's palette sits at 90. */\n    top?: number\n    /** Corner radius in CSS px (default 12; the palette's frame is 14). */\n    radius?: number\n    /** A sheet docked to the window's right edge under the header (R2App's review sheet, 620px wide, full height). */\n    sheet?: boolean\n    /**\n     * The control focus returns to on close when the opener itself will be gone\n     * by then (a menu item that closes with its menu as the dialog opens): an\n     * explicit surviving target instead of whatever had focus at mount.\n     */\n    returnFocus?: HTMLElement | null\n    'data-slot'?: string\n}\n\nconst FOCUSABLE = 'a[href], button:not([disabled]), input:not([disabled]), select:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled]), [tabindex]:not([tabindex=\"-1\"])'\n\n/**\n * One topmost modal (I8): dialogs register on a shell-wide stack; only the\n * last is interactive. Lower dialogs are inert and aria-hidden, Tab and\n * Shift-Tab stay inside the topmost dialog, Escape closes the topmost only,\n * focus moves into the dialog on open and back to the opener on close. The\n * page behind every dialog is made inert by the shell (`useModalsOpen`).\n * The dialog element handles its own keys; the topmost dialog also listens\n * on the window for Escape alone, for when focus has left it (a native\n * sheet returned focus elsewhere), and closes only itself.\n */\nexport function Modal({ label, onClose, children, width = 560, padding = 20, top, radius = 12, sheet = false, returnFocus = null, ...rest }: ModalProps) {\n    const id = useId()\n    const pushModal = useShellStore((s) => s.pushModal)\n    const popModal = useShellStore((s) => s.popModal)\n    const modals = useShellStore((s) => s.modals)\n    const topmost = modals.length > 0 && modals[modals.length - 1] === id\n    const dialog = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n    const opener = useRef<HTMLElement | null>(null)\n    const returnRef = useRef(returnFocus)\n    returnRef.current = returnFocus\n    const focusedOnce = useRef(false)\n\n    useEffect(() => {\n        opener.current = document.activeElement instanceof HTMLElement ? document.activeElement : null\n        pushModal(id)\n        return () => {\n            popModal(id)\n            // After the commit: the page behind is still inert during cleanup,\n            // and an inert ancestor refuses focus (observed in WebKit).\n            const target = returnRef.current ?? opener.current\n            queueMicrotask(() => {\n                // Only when nothing else took focus meanwhile (⌘T replacing the\n                // palette hands focus to the tenant list, which must keep it).\n                const active = document.activeElement\n                if (active && active !== document.body) return\n                // The opener may be gone (a \"Finish rotation…\" that completed):\n                // focus the page heading rather than leave it on nothing.\n                if (target?.isConnected) target.focus()\n                else document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('main h1[tabindex=\"-1\"]')?.focus()\n            })\n        }\n    }, [id, pushModal, popModal])\n\n    useEffect(() => {\n        // Initial focus goes into the dialog once, when it opens. Regaining the\n        // top after a higher dialog closes must not refocus: that dialog is\n        // restoring its own opener, which may be any control here.\n        if (!topmost || focusedOnce.current) return\n        const node = dialog.current\n        if (!node) return\n        focusedOnce.current = true\n        if (!node.contains(document.activeElement)) {\n            // A declared initial control first (wherever it sits), else the first focusable.\n            const first = node.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[autofocus]') ?? node.querySelector<HTMLElement>(FOCUSABLE)\n            ;(first ?? node).focus()\n        }\n    }, [topmost])\n\n    // Escape still closes the topmost dialog when focus has left it (a\n    // native sheet returning focus to the page body, a click on the scrim's\n    // edge): the dialog's own handler stops the event first when it has focus.\n    const closeRef = useRef(onClose)\n    closeRef.current = onClose\n    useEffect(() => {\n        if (!topmost) return\n        const onWindowKey = (event: globalThis.KeyboardEvent) => {\n            if (event.key !== 'Escape' || event.defaultPrevented) return\n            const node = dialog.current\n            if (node && node.contains(document.activeElement)) return\n            event.preventDefault()\n            closeRef.current()\n        }\n        window.addEventListener('keydown', onWindowKey)\n        return () => window.removeEventListener('keydown', onWindowKey)\n    }, [topmost])\n\n    const onKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\n        if (!topmost) return\n        if (event.key === 'Escape') {\n            event.preventDefault()\n            event.stopPropagation()\n            onClose()\n            return\n        }\n        if (event.key === 'Tab') {\n            // Keyboard interaction stays inside the topmost dialog.\n            const node = dialog.current\n            if (!node) return\n            const items = Array.from(node.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(FOCUSABLE)).filter((el) => !el.hasAttribute('hidden') && el.getAttribute('aria-hidden') !== 'true')\n            if (items.length === 0) {\n                event.preventDefault()\n                node.focus()\n                return\n            }\n            const first = items[0] as HTMLElement\n            const last = items[items.length - 1] as HTMLElement\n            const active = document.activeElement\n            if (event.shiftKey && (active === first || active === node)) {\n                event.preventDefault()\n                last.focus()\n            } else if (!event.shiftKey && active === last) {\n                event.preventDefault()\n                first.focus()\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    return (\n        <div\n            className={sheet ? 'fixed z-50 flex justify-end' : 'fixed inset-0 z-50 grid place-items-start justify-center'}\n            style={sheet ? { inset: 'var(--v2-header, 56px) 0 0 0' } : { paddingTop: top ?? '4vh' }}\n            data-v2-scrim=''\n            aria-hidden={topmost ? undefined : true}\n            inert={topmost ? undefined : true}\n            onMouseDown={() => topmost && onClose()}\n        >\n            <div\n                ref={dialog}\n                role='dialog'\n                aria-modal={topmost ? 'true' : undefined}\n                aria-label={label}\n                tabIndex={-1}\n                data-slot={rest['data-slot'] ?? 'modal'}\n                data-topmost={topmost ? 'true' : 'false'}\n                onKeyDown={onKeyDown}\n                onMouseDown={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}\n                className='border'\n                // Bounded to the viewport: a tall dialog scrolls inside itself, so its\n                // actions stay reachable at the minimum window size and 200% zoom.\n                style={\n                    sheet\n                        ? { width: `min(${width}px, 100vw)`, height: '100%', overflowY: 'auto', padding, borderRadius: 0, borderLeft: '1px solid var(--v2-rule)', boxShadow: '-18px 0 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.18)', background: 'var(--v2-bg)', borderWidth: 0, color: 'var(--v2-ink)' }\n                        : { width: `min(${width}px, 92vw)`, maxHeight: '92vh', overflowY: 'auto', padding, borderRadius: radius, boxShadow: '0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)', borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', color: 'var(--v2-ink)' }\n                }\n            >\n                {children}\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\n/** Whether any modal is open: the shell makes the page behind it inert. */\nexport function useModalsOpen(): boolean {\n    return useShellStore((s) => s.modals.length > 0)\n}\nimport { type ReactNode, useEffect, useId, useRef, useState } from 'react'\nimport { Button, Callout, Input, cn } from '@ai-security-academy/presentation'\nimport { AlertTriangle, Info, KeyRound } from 'lucide-react'\nimport type {\n    ChangeAction,\n    ChangeDraft,\n    ChangeFailure,\n    ChangeKind,\n    ChangeProblem,\n    ChangeResultView,\n    ChangeReviewView,\n    ContextRef,\n    Provisioning,\n    ScopeCleanup,\n    StagedFileFailure,\n    StagedFileView,\n    StepState,\n    WorkspaceRef,\n} from '@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts'\nimport { type Dispatch, outcomeMessage } from '../tenants/dispatch'\nimport { MANAGEMENT_FAILURE_TEXT } from './management-read'\n\n/** What the operator chose to change (body is the editor's initial text). */\nexport interface ChangeTarget {\n    kind: ChangeKind\n    action: ChangeAction\n    target: string\n    title: string\n    body: string\n    /** A Gateway change inside the chosen workspace: its native reference. */\n    workspace?: WorkspaceRef\n    /** A Gateway draft kept on this Mac that this change edits (C17). */\n    draftId?: string\n    /** Why it cannot be reviewed now (the draft's workspace is not chosen). */\n    reviewBlocked?: string\n}\n\nconst PROBLEM_TEXT: Record<ChangeProblem, string> = {\n    unsupported: 'This change is not supported.',\n    target: 'The item to change is missing or invalid.',\n    body: 'The draft must be a single JSON object.',\n    contract: 'The draft does not match what the service accepts. Check the field names and values.',\n    description: 'A custom topic description can have at most 240 characters.',\n    rotation: 'Key rotation must be 30, 90 or 180 days.',\n    keyFields: 'Enter the key name, application, environment, cloud provider and deployment profile.',\n    applicationExists: 'An application with that name already exists. Add a key version to it instead.',\n    keyExists: 'An API key with that name already exists.',\n    inventoryLimit: 'The inventory is too large to check completely, so the change was not prepared.',\n    deploymentProfile: 'The deployment profile was not found exactly once.',\n    sourceMismatch: 'The key version must use the existing key’s application.',\n    notFound: 'The item is no longer in the service’s inventory.',\n    dataProfile:\n        'The data profile is incomplete: check the name (at most 32 characters), its rules, techniques, confidence levels and occurrence bounds.',\n    dictionaryFile: 'The keyword list must be non-empty text of at most 65,536 characters.',\n    fileName: 'The original file name cannot contain slashes, quotes or control characters (at most 255 characters).',\n    stagedFile: 'The chosen file is no longer available. Choose it again.',\n    previewOnly: 'Directional settings and customized prompt-injection modes were local previews in the previous desktop; remove them from the draft. They are never sent.',\n    credentialPolicy:\n        'Credentials are never part of a draft: remove keys, secret mappings and credential-bearing settings. They are entered only where the desktop protects them.',\n    protectedConfiguration:\n        'This item holds credentials the change would replace or lose, so it cannot be changed here. Change its other fields, or its credentials where they are protected.',\n    workspaceMismatch: 'The draft names a different workspace. Changes apply only to the workspace chosen here.',\n    configuration: 'The settings do not meet the provider family’s or the guardrail catalog’s rules.',\n    scopeExists: 'That IAM scope already exists. Choose to reuse it, or name a new one.',\n    scopeMissing: 'That IAM scope does not exist, so it cannot be reused.',\n    referenced: 'Other configuration still references this item, so it was not changed.',\n}\n\nconst STAGED_TEXT: Record<StagedFileFailure, string> = {\n    tooLarge: 'That file is larger than 65,536 characters.',\n    notText: 'That file is not UTF-8 text.',\n    empty: 'That file has no keywords.',\n    unreadable: 'That file could not be read.',\n}\n\nexport function changeFailureText(failure: ChangeFailure): string {\n    switch (failure.kind) {\n        case 'problem':\n            return PROBLEM_TEXT[failure.problem]\n        case 'conflict':\n            return 'The item changed since it was reviewed. Review the change again.'\n        case 'service':\n            // A change is stopped by the operator or a tenant change, never\n            // \"read\".\n            return failure.failure === 'cancelled'\n                ? 'The desktop stopped waiting for this change.'\n                : MANAGEMENT_FAILURE_TEXT[failure.failure]\n        case 'expired':\n            return 'This review expired before it was applied. Review the change again.'\n        case 'capacity':\n            return 'The desktop could not start the change right now, so nothing was sent. Review it again.'\n        case 'workspaceChanged':\n            return 'Another workspace was chosen before this change was sent, so nothing was sent. Review it again in the workspace it is for.'\n    }\n}\n\nexport const CHANGE_NOUN: Record<ChangeKind, string> = {\n    profiles: 'security profile',\n    topics: 'custom topic',\n    applications: 'application',\n    apiKeys: 'API key',\n    dataPatterns: 'data pattern',\n    dataProfiles: 'data profile',\n    filteringProfiles: 'data filtering profile',\n    dictionaries: 'dictionary',\n    gatewayWorkspaces: 'workspace',\n    gatewayProviders: 'provider',\n    gatewayRoutes: 'route',\n    gatewayGuardrails: 'guardrail',\n    gatewayServiceKeys: 'service key',\n    gatewayUserKeys: 'user key',\n    gatewayIntegrations: 'integration',\n}\n\n/** How a change's action reads in a result line. */\nexport function verbOf(kind: ChangeKind, action: ChangeAction): string {\n    if (kind === 'gatewayWorkspaces' && action === 'delete') return 'Archive'\n    if (kind === 'gatewayWorkspaces' && action === 'create') return 'Provision'\n    if (action === 'models') return 'Change models of'\n    return action.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + action.slice(1)\n}\n\nexport const isGatewayKind = (kind: ChangeKind) => kind.startsWith('gateway')\n\nconst TEXTAREA = cn(\n    'rounded-academy-md bg-academy-bg-inset border-academy-rule focus-visible:border-academy-accent-ring w-full border px-3.5 py-2.5',\n    'text-academy-ink min-h-48 resize-y font-mono text-[12px] leading-snug'\n)\n\nfunction Json({ label, text }: { label: string; text: string | null }) {\n    if (text === null) return null\n    let pretty = text\n    try {\n        pretty = JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(text), null, 2)\n    } catch {\n        // Shown as received.\n    }\n    return (\n        <div className='flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-1'>\n            <span className='text-academy-ink-soft text-[12px] font-medium'>{label}</span>\n            <pre className='bg-academy-bg-inset rounded-academy-md max-h-72 overflow-auto p-3 font-mono text-[11px] break-all whitespace-pre-wrap'>\n                {pretty}\n            </pre>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\ninterface WorkbenchProps {\n    change: ChangeTarget\n    review: ChangeReviewView | null\n    /** The dictionary keyword file chosen in the native sheet, if any. */\n    staged?: StagedFileView | null\n    context: ContextRef\n    dispatch: Dispatch\n    onClose: () => void\n    /** Keeps the edited text as a local draft (C17); called after edits pause. */\n    onDraft?: (body: string) => void\n    /** Set to the workbench's draft flush, for a host that removes it (Close, Escape, the scrim) before React's cleanup can read the editor. */\n    flushRef?: React.MutableRefObject<(() => void) | null>\n    /** Shown under the editor (where the draft is kept). */\n    note?: ReactNode\n    /** v2 (C31, I3): Apply stays disabled until the typed name matches the review's. */\n    requireTyped?: boolean\n}\n\n/** How long typing pauses before a draft is kept. */\nconst DRAFT_PAUSE_MS = 800\n\n/** Splits a dictionary body into its metadata JSON and keyword text. */\nfunction dictionaryParts(body: string): { metadata: string; keywords: string } {\n    try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(body) as { metadata?: unknown; file?: unknown }\n        return { metadata: JSON.stringify(parsed.metadata ?? {}, null, 2), keywords: typeof parsed.file === 'string' ? parsed.file : '' }\n    } catch {\n        return { metadata: body, keywords: '' }\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * Edit, review and apply one Runtime change. The editor is uncontrolled:\n * Review and Apply read its current text at the moment they are pressed\n * (no debounced copy), and Rust compares Apply's text with the reviewed\n * draft. While the native confirmation is open the editor is read-only and\n * the main window is held by the sheet.\n */\nexport function ChangeWorkbench({ change, review, staged = null, context, dispatch, onClose, onDraft, flushRef, note, requireTyped = false }: WorkbenchProps) {\n    const ids = useId()\n    const [typedText, setTypedText] = useState('')\n    const heading = useRef<HTMLHeadingElement>(null)\n    const editor = useRef<HTMLTextAreaElement>(null)\n    const keywords = useRef<HTMLTextAreaElement>(null)\n    const [useFile, setUseFile] = useState(false)\n    const dictionary = change.kind === 'dictionaries'\n    const parts = dictionary ? dictionaryParts(change.body) : null\n    const typed = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)\n    const [message, setMessage] = useState<string | null>(null)\n    const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false)\n    const mine =\n        review && review.kind === change.kind && review.action === change.action && review.target === change.target\n            ? review\n            : null\n    const confirming = mine?.state === 'confirming'\n    const blocked = (mine?.references.length ?? 0) > 0\n    const deletes = change.action === 'delete'\n\n    // The chosen file is used only once one is actually staged; a cancelled\n    // or failed choice leaves the typed keywords in use.\n    const fileReady = staged?.state === 'ready' && !!staged.token\n    const usingFile = useFile && fileReady\n    // Opening a change moves focus to it.\n            let metadata: unknown\n            try {\n                metadata = JSON.parse(text)\n            } catch {\n                metadata = null\n            }\n            if (typeof metadata !== 'object' || metadata === null || Array.isArray(metadata)) {\n                setMessage('The dictionary metadata must be one JSON object.')\n                return null\n            }\n            body = JSON.stringify(\n                usingFile && staged?.token\n                    ? { metadata, fileRef: staged.token }\n                    : { metadata, file: keywords.current?.value ?? '' }\n            )\n        }\n        const captured: ChangeDraft = { kind: change.kind, action: change.action, target: change.target, body }\n        if (change.workspace) captured.workspace = change.workspace\n        return captured\n    }\n\n    async function chooseFile() {\n        setAwaitingFile(true)\n        setMessage(outcomeMessage(await dispatch({ kind: 'chooseDictionaryFile', context })))\n    }\n\n    async function prepare() {\n        // The reviewed text is kept first, so a later settlement finds it.\n        keepDraft()\n        setMessage(null)\n        const captured = draft()\n        if (!captured) return\n        setBusy(true)\n        const outcome = await dispatch({ kind: 'reviewChange', context, draft: captured })\n        setBusy(false)\n        setMessage(outcomeMessage(outcome))\n    }\n\n    async function apply() {\n        if (!mine) return\n        setMessage(null)\n        const captured = draft()\n        if (!captured) return\n        setBusy(true)\n        const outcome = await dispatch({\n            kind: 'requestApply',\n            review: mine.review,\n            draft: captured,\n            confirmation: typed.current?.value ?? '',\n        })\n        setBusy(false)\n        if (outcome.kind === 'refused' && outcome.refusal === 'reviewInvalid') {\n            setMessage('The draft changed since it was reviewed, or the review expired. Review the change again.')\n        } else if (outcome.kind === 'refused' && outcome.refusal === 'invalidInput') {\n            setMessage(`Type ${mine.confirmation ?? 'the confirmation'} exactly to confirm.`)\n        } else setMessage(outcomeMessage(outcome))\n    }\n\n    async function discard() {\n        keepDraft()\n        if (mine) await dispatch({ kind: 'discardChange', review: mine.review })\n        onClose()\n    }\n\n    return (\n        <section\n            aria-labelledby={`${ids}-heading`}\n            data-slot='change-workbench'\n            className='border-academy-rule flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-[12px] border p-5'\n        >\n            <h2 id={`${ids}-heading`} ref={heading} tabIndex={-1} className='text-academy-ink text-[15px] font-semibold outline-none'>\n                {change.title}\n            </h2>\n            {deletes ? (\n                <p className='text-[13px]'>Review what will be removed before applying.</p>\n            ) : (\n                <div className='flex flex-col gap-1'>\n                    <label htmlFor={`${ids}-editor`} className='text-academy-ink text-[13px] font-medium'>\n                        {dictionary ? 'dictionary metadata (JSON)' : `${CHANGE_NOUN[change.kind]} draft (JSON)`}\n                    </label>\n                    <textarea\n                        ref={editor}\n                        id={`${ids}-editor`}\n                        defaultValue={parts ? parts.metadata : change.body}\n                        readOnly={confirming}\n                        spellCheck={false}\n                        aria-describedby={`${ids}-editor-hint`}\n                        className={TEXTAREA}\n                        onInput={edited}\n                        data-slot='change-editor'\n                    />\n                    <p id={`${ids}-editor-hint`} className='text-academy-ink-faint text-[12px]'>\n                        Authorship is set from the management client. Server-assigned fields are ignored.\n                        {change.kind === 'profiles'\n                            ? ' Directional settings and customized prompt-injection modes were local previews in the previous desktop; they are not part of a draft and are never sent.'\n                            : ''}\n                    </p>\n                    {note}\n                    {parts ? (\n                        <fieldset className='mt-2 flex flex-col gap-2' data-slot='dictionary-keywords'>\n                            <legend className='text-academy-ink text-[13px] font-medium'>Keywords</legend>\n                            <label className='flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 text-[13px]'>\n                                <input\n                                    type='radio'\n                                    name={`${ids}-source`}\n                                    checked={!usingFile}\n                                    disabled={confirming}\n                                    onChange={() => setUseFile(false)}\n                                    className='size-4 accent-[var(--academy-accent)]'\n                                />\n                                Type them (one per line)\n                            </label>\n                            <textarea\n                                ref={keywords}\n                                aria-label='Dictionary keywords, one per line'\n                                defaultValue={parts.keywords}\n                                readOnly={confirming}\n                                disabled={usingFile}\n                                spellCheck={false}\n                                className={TEXTAREA}\n                                data-slot='dictionary-text'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/planning/reviews/C30/owner-override-2026-11-02.md docs/planning/reviews/C31/attempt-05/acceptance.md; sed -n '130,195p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/workbench_domain/send.rs; sed -n '525,561p' packages/desktop-contracts/src/client.ts; sed -n '180,245p' crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs; cat docs/planning/evidence/C31/remediation-attempt-05/R2-native-assertions.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/planning/reviews/C30/owner-override-2026-11-02.md docs/planning/reviews/C31/attempt-05/acceptance.md; sed -n '130,195p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/workbench_domain/send.rs; sed -n '525,561p' packages/desktop-contracts/src/client.ts; sed -n '180,245p' crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs; cat docs/planning/evidence/C31/remediation-attempt-05/R2-native-assertions.md\"","aggregated_output":"# C30 — owner closure, 2026-11-02\n\nThe owner's direction, verbatim: \"hey. no more C30. it has full passing. stop working on it.\"\n\nThe owner then objected to days of repeated testing and asked to finish P09. Root stopped the C30 worker by interrupting its saved-session primary at 2026-11-02T11:15:44Z. No further C30 implementation, coverage expansion, native captures, tests or re-review are authorized for this baseline, including reopening the same findings through another review.\n\nC30 is complete by the owner's decision. This is an explicit exception to its remaining D034 push-to-9 requirement, analogous to C41's existing owner exception. It satisfies C30's predecessor/member completion requirement for C31 and P09. It does not waive actual C31, C32 or P09 independent reviews.\n\nThe raw attempt-12 verdict remains unchanged: architecture 9, behavior 9, authority_security 9, validation 8, overall 8; no blockers; recommendation fail. Accepted at eight under D034 in commit 4578d2f5. This note does not assign a new independent numeric score or claim the unperformed native scenarios happened. R1/R2/E1/E2 remain preserved in that verdict as limitations the owner has closed for this baseline.\n\nThe implemented save-order remediation is committed at 2275f046. G7's 19 mapped native-driver results and all 18 repository checks of run-attempt-07 passed. C30 performance attempt-03 retained ten measured samples, p95 23.69475 ms against 100 ms. Passing results remain bound to their original inputs and are not relabeled. C29 attempt-10 independently passed 9/9/9/9/9 on this application baseline.\n\nApplication executable SHA-256: 2791b5a1eaf6b9268e0574502c62a20f3027fd2b76ff9ed08289eef1f56147ea.\nCanonical full fixture bundle SHA-256: c673feed3aa0948e643a2c4bf23b793364fb6a6a12b1cbc2f0de877757c288f9.\nCompiled-input digest: f5f26271b8823df8a2b5299417146784d345d4e04f8b59341706e6a41750210d.\nRaw verdict: docs/planning/reviews/C30/attempt-12/verdict-returned.json\nRaw verdict SHA-256: f49d633701dcb7d606ca176f3edaeee8d435866e1ee0d142c540029c3035d2ec\nHEAD when recorded: 4578d2f509ce09bf2f929ce6b77dd66136b06ac1\nRecorded UTC: 2026-11-02T11:31:34.376687+00:00\n\nProceed directly to C31, C32 and actual P09 phase review using passing evidence. Disclose this and C41's exceptions in their packets; preserve raw reviews and source scopes. Do not restart C29 or repeat native, Rust or repository check suites for this administrative closure.\n# C31 attempt-05 D034 acceptance\n\nActual independent review scored9/8/8/8/8 with no blockers, acceptedat8 under standingD034. Raw verdict, requiredfixesR1/R2 and gapE1 remain unchanged. Native page-teardown authority retirement and missing C31 native assertions are in focused remediation; actual re-review at9 remains required. No C30 work is reopened; its explicit owner all9 override stands for P09. C26 controllercompletion, phase sign-off and release remain separate.\n    /// Advanced by every reset: work planned in an earlier epoch was\n    /// retired and neither stores nor publishes anything.\n    epoch: u64,\n    /// Held shared by each private-storage step of a send and exclusively\n    /// by reset from before its purge to its end.\n    fence: Arc<tokio::sync::RwLock<()>>,\n    /// Holds each Send between its document capture and its rendering\n    /// while a test holds it, and counts those waiting (fixture builds).\n    #[cfg(feature = \"test-fixtures\")]\n    planning: (Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<()>>, Arc<AtomicU64>),\n}\n\nimpl Sending {\n    /// Reset: running requests are cancelled; tokens, cookies, reviews and\n    /// histories are forgotten (their files go with the private folder).\n    pub(super) fn clear(&mut self) {\n        self.epoch += 1;\n        for active in self.runs.values() {\n            active.cancel.cancel();\n        }\n        self.review = None;\n        self.tokens.clear();\n        self.jars.clear();\n        self.histories.clear();\n    }\n\n    /// The fence reset holds exclusively while it purges.\n    pub(in crate::authority) fn fence(&self) -> Arc<tokio::sync::RwLock<()>> {\n        Arc::clone(&self.fence)\n    }\n\n    #[cfg(feature = \"test-fixtures\")]\n    pub(in crate::authority) fn planning(&self) -> (Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<()>>, Arc<AtomicU64>) {\n        (Arc::clone(&self.planning.0), Arc::clone(&self.planning.1))\n    }\n\n    /// A collection was closed or another opened.\n    pub(super) fn leave(&mut self) {\n        self.review = None;\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn running(&self) -> Vec<RunningView> {\n        self.runs\n            .iter()\n            .map(|(run, a)| RunningView {\n                run: run.clone(),\n                request: a.request.clone(),\n                method: a.method.clone(),\n                bytes: a.progress.load(Ordering::Relaxed),\n            })\n            .collect()\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn review(&self) -> Option<SendReviewView> {\n        self.review.as_ref().map(|p| p.view.clone())\n    }\n\n    /// A workbench secret is about to be replaced or removed: what was\n    /// planned or reviewed with it no longer goes.\n    pub(super) fn secret_changed(&mut self, collection: &str, reference: &str) {\n        self.generation += 1;\n        self.secret_generations.insert(\n            (collection.to_owned(), reference.to_owned()),\n            self.generation,\n        );\n    }\n                    (!p.readOnly || t.actions.length === 0) &&\n                    Array.isArray(t.denied) &&\n                    t.denied.every((d: unknown) => isPair(d) && isString((d as Record<string, unknown>).reason)) &&\n                    optional(isString, t.resource)\n            )\n    )\n}\n\nconst ROTATION_STAGES: readonly string[] = ['issuanceUnconfirmed', 'issued', 'resumed', 'acknowledged', 'removalUnconfirmed', 'complete']\n/** One key rotation (C31, I7): its two labelled timestamps and stage. */\nfunction isRotationView(value: unknown): boolean {\n    const isKey = (k: unknown) => isRecord(k) && isString(k.id) && typeof k.name === 'string'\n    return (\n        isRecord(value) &&\n        isString(value.application) &&\n        isKey(value.oldKey) &&\n        optional(isKey, value.newKey) &&\n        oneOf(ROTATION_STAGES, value.stage) &&\n        optional(isString, value.issuedBy) &&\n        isCount(value.issuedAt) &&\n        optional(isCount, value.deploymentAcknowledgedAt) &&\n        optional(isCount, value.oldKeyRemovedAt) &&\n        optional(isString, value.removalRejected) &&\n        typeof value.unsaved === 'boolean' &&\n        // Complete means read back gone, with its time; otherwise that time is unset.\n        ((value.stage === 'complete') === (value.oldKeyRemovedAt !== null)) &&\n        // The held key is offered only while it may be revealed: issued, or\n        // issued but not yet confirmed by readback (C31, I6).\n        (value.stage === 'issued' || value.stage === 'issuanceUnconfirmed' || value.issuedBy === null) &&\n        // Nothing is claimed about a key an unconfirmed issuance has not read back.\n        (value.stage !== 'issuanceUnconfirmed' || value.newKey === null)\n    )\n}\n\nfunction isScanRecord(value: unknown): boolean {\n    if (\n        !isRecord(value) ||\n/// A Runtime API key named by its identifier and name (never a secret).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct KeyRef {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub name: String,\n}\n\n/// Whether the additional key's issuance was confirmed by readback (C31).\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub enum RotationIssuance {\n    Confirmed,\n    /// The version settled unknown: a key is confirmed only once the key\n    /// inventory shows one for the application besides the old key.\n    Unconfirmed,\n}\n\n/// Where the old key's removal stands (C31).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n#[serde(tag = \"state\", rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub enum RotationRemoval {\n    Pending,\n    /// Sent but not read back absent: reconciled by a complete inventory.\n    Unconfirmed,\n    /// Refused or failed: the reminder stays, the completion time unset.\n    Rejected {\n        reason: String,\n    },\n    Done,\n}\n\n/// One Runtime API key rotation of a tenant (C31, I7), persisted so its two\n/// timestamps are stored once and survive reads, switches and relaunches.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct Rotation {\n    pub application: String,\n    pub old_key: KeyRef,\n    pub new_key: Option<KeyRef>,\n    pub issuance: RotationIssuance,\n    /// The change result that issued the key (its one-time secret lives\n    /// there, for the context it was applied in, never here). Session-only:\n    /// operation IDs restart with the core, so a relaunch never restores\n    /// this link (a reused ID must not point at another key; C31).\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    #[ts(skip)]\n    pub issued_by: Option<String>,\n    /// The key name the issuing review named: the only key that can confirm\n    /// an unconfirmed issuance.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub pending_name: Option<String>,\n    pub issued_at: u32,\n    /// The operator's local statement that the application uses the new key.\n    pub deployment_acknowledged_at: Option<u32>,\n    pub removal: RotationRemoval,\n    /// When the old key was read back absent (remote readback).\n    pub old_key_removed_at: Option<u32>,\n}\n\n/// Stable identifier of a top-level desktop feature destination.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub enum FeatureId {\n    /// v2 only (C28): the tenant's Home.\n    Home,\n# C31 attempt-05 R2/E1 native assertion correction\n\nRaw attempt-05 verdict and historical native failures remain unchanged. This changes qualification requirements and future driver observations; it does not call old failed records passed or claim fresh native execution.\n\n- C31-N01 now requires its own inventory assertions plus C39-N01/N03. Agentic products must contain only their gate and header. Runtime key details must contain exactly their admitted actions. Gateway checks operate within the actual product-card subtree, require both Service keys and User keys lists, open every returned key detail, reject Issue additional key / Finish rotation there, and retain each source tree/capture. A missing card, table, detail or required assertion cannot satisfy a negative check.\n- C31-N04 now requires its own accessibility observations plus current C39-N02/N04 review/board facts on the same executable. The C31 driver focuses the actual Runtime card header rather than the navigation-rail namesake, retains the focus walk and modal/focus-return trees, and requires exactly one topmost review modal. All original review ring/status/Reduce Motion/restoration/reminder requirements remain enforced.\n- C39 Gateway route/key actions are scoped to that product's table/detail; an open Runtime detail can no longer stand in for a Gateway result. Both key-kind lists and every returned detail restriction are mandatory for C39-N03. Custom-topic detail actions are checked exactly.\n\nFocused verification: nine Python unittest methods passed, including Runtime/Gateway contamination, forbidden Gateway controls, missing context/detail, actual card-header selection, gate-only surfaces, mandatory per-kind/per-row facts and missing/failed/stale native-record controls. The production mapper previously required C31-N02/N03 only; it now requires all four unretired C31 checks. See R2-focused-results.json. Syntax and git diff --check passed. No native UI run, app build, Rust suite or full repository suite was performed in this isolated worktree.\n\nC30 owner closure and all C30 mapping entries are untouched. No C30 measurement, scenario, capture matrix or raw verdict was changed or run. Root's integration author owns the actual current-source qualification and new independent C31 review.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
